            <ArticleTitle>A rare case: surviving acute left main coronary artery occlusion in Kawasaki's disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1323-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of cardiogenic shock due to acute thrombotic occlusion of the left main coronary artery in Kawasaki's aneurysmal coronary artery disease. The patient was treated with PTCA as a bridge to CABG. Because of a persistent low-output syndrome, orthotopic heart transplantation was successfully performed three days later. The patient is alive and well one year after the event.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
